                          "text":  "Hello. You found me. I am the bottom half of a spacecraft called Eagle, and I have been sitting very still since July 1969.\n\nMy job was easy to say and hard to do: carry two people down to the Moon and set them down gently. On the way down the computer flashed alarms, and Neil Armstrong took over the steering to fly us past a field of boulders. We landed with very little fuel to spare. Then he said it: \"Houston, Tranquility Base here. The Eagle has landed.\"",
